From 0602281bb23c7ad4a1efe62b2e5d213f9a141f88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwqgong-ui <248246420+qwqgong-ui@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 20:21:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] patch: preserve remote UDP destination identity

Keep remote-capable proxy UDP on FQDN while preserving upstream DIRECT behavior: resolve with the built-in direct resolver, send a native UDP address, and keep exact IP NAT mappings.

Retain conservative FQDN reply restoration for XUDP and Hysteria2 without applying domain transport semantics to locally resolved outbounds.

DIRECT intentionally keeps upstream local-DNS and native UDP address semantics.
